#---
# purpose: "a closure destructured out of a tuple is callable even when the sibling field is discarded"
#---
#
# # tuple_field_closure_call_unused_field
#
# The companion to `tuple_field_closure_call` with one field taken away.
# `call_pair` binds the lambda and discards the integer beside it, so the body
# projects field 0 and nothing at all projects field 1.
#
# A consumer states what it needs field by field, and a field nobody reads is
# simply not asked for. That has to leave the field it does read exactly as
# demanding as it would be in a body that read both: the lambda is still used
# as a callable, still names one target, and still has that target's capture to
# carry. Reading fewer fields is not evidence about the fields still read.
#
# The claim here is one value equality, so the program checks itself with
# `assert` and prints nothing. There is no golden and no oracle: a failure
# aborts, on every path.
defp pair_adder(n), do: {fn x -> x + n end, n}

defp call_pair({f, _k}), do: f.(7)

def main() do
  assert(call_pair(pair_adder(5)) == 12, "the projected lambda carries its capture through the unread sibling")
end
